message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EvoBot: BDDL formal spec + reusable skills for the LIBERO benchmark"
authors:
- family-names: "Li"
  given-names: "Feida"
  email: "1607741781@qq.com"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-01"
url: "https://github.com/ABC12345anouys/EvoBot"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  An execution stack for the LIBERO robot manipulation benchmark. BDDL task
  definitions are treated as a formal spec: predicates are parsed into ordered
  subgoals, an LLM performs a one-off predicate-level decomposition that is
  frozen into version-controlled YAML (so runtime uses zero tokens), subgoals
  map to reusable parameterized skills, and skill failures return failure
  mechanisms that drive re-planning.
